Subject: ECON/SPACE: Sell the Universe Whole

First of all, any attempt to 'sell off' anthing beyond the 
Solar System is as presumpuous as the UN was in authoring the
'Moon Treaty'.  You and they assume that the rest of the Universe
is not occupied by others, and thus a subject for division by
humans.

Second, here is an alternative approach:

Take the Moon, for example.  A set of individuals establish
a lunar development company.  Each contributes capital to the
company, and gets some region of the Moon as 'his' in return.

The company and the individuals contract to recognize and 
protect each other's claims to the respective portions of the
Moon.  Non-participants in the company are ignored.

In reality, the Moon is probably too big and too close for
a non-government project to effectively defend, so the
same idea applied to a more manageably sized area (a 10 kilometer
square on the lunar surface, or a small asteroid) would
be more reasonable.

